026-27","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56721/56721.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Eighty fire safety remedial actions overdue at end of Q1, including 27 high-priority items.","lead":"Overdue fire safety compliance actions represent regulatory risk for a registered social housing provider and potential intervention exposure.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"FPSC Report -Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56721/56721.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Finance and Performance Scrutiny Sub-Committee","paper_title":"FPSC Report -Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56721/56721.pdf","headline":"Temporary accommodation and bed-and-breakfast use above target; council investing in own-built units to manage costs.","detail":"Average households in temporary accommodation 128 against target 120; average in bed-and-breakfast 30 against target 20, both higher than same quarter last year. Council reported options to Cabinet to expand Council-owned TA to reduce costs rather than overall numbers. First eight Council-owned units acquired May 2026; further eight due to start by November with completion autumn 2027.","category":"capital","matters":"Demonstrates higher-than-budgeted demand for homelessness services and council's capital investment response; material to HRA financial position and cashflow planning.","figures":"TA: 128 vs 120 target (up from 101); B&B: 30 vs 20 target (up from 10); 8 units acquired May 2026, 8 more starting November 2026","quote":"The Council continues to support households into long-term housing and has reported options to Cabinet to expand Council-owned TA, reducing costs rather than overall numbers. The first eight Council-owned units were acquired in early May 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Finance and Performance Scrutiny Sub-Committee","paper_title":"FPSC Report -Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56721/56721.pdf","headline":"Thirty-one water safety remedial actions overdue at end of Q1, including 12 high-priority items.","detail":"4 of 35 Water Risk Assessment remedial actions completed on time; 31 remain overdue but progressed through agreed programme. Overdue portfolio comprises 12 high-priority, 13 medium-priority and 6 low-priority actions, with most approved for completion and awaiting tenant or leaseholder access.","category":"governance","matters":"Overdue water safety compliance actions represent regulatory risk for a registered social housing provider and potential financial liability for remediation.","figures":"31 overdue of 35 total WRA actions; 12 high-priority overdue; 11% of actions completed on time","quote":"At the end of June, 4 out of 35 outstanding remedial Water Risk Assessment (WRA) actions were still within target for completion (11%). This means that 31 actions were 'overdue' but being progressed through an agreed programme of works.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Finance and Performance Scrutiny Sub-Committee","paper_title":"FPSC Report -Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56721/56721.pdf","headline":"Eighty fire safety remedial actions overdue at end of Q1, including 27 high-priority items.","detail":"72 of 152 Fire Risk Assessment remedial actions completed on time; 80 remain overdue but being progressed through agreed programme. Overdue portfolio comprises 27 high-priority, 4 medium-priority and 49 low-priority actions distributed across Fire Door Remedials, Compliance and Surveyors/Neighbourhood teams.","category":"governance","matters":"Overdue fire safety compliance actions represent regulatory risk for a registered social housing provider and potential intervention exposure.","figures":"80 overdue of 152 total FRA actions; 27 high-priority overdue; 47% of actions completed on time","quote":"At the end of June, 72 out of 152 outstanding remedial Fire Risk Assessment (FRA) actions were still within target for completion (47%). This means that 80 actions were 'overdue', but being progressed through an agreed programme of works.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Finance and Performance Scrutiny Sub-Committee","paper_title":"FPSC Report -Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56721/56721.pdf","headline":"485 housing properties fall short of Decent Homes Standard against regulatory target of 99%.","detail":"86% of council housing properties meet the Decent Homes Standard against annual target of 99%. 485 of 3,413 applicable properties do not meet standard: 412 are in current year works programme, 43 under review, 30 with work orders raised. Council has agreed proactive plan with Regulator of Social Housing for potential 2027-28 failures.","category":"governance","matters":"Represents a material regulatory compliance obligation with the social housing regulator and direct financial liability for remedial works.","figures":"86% vs 99% target; 485 of 3,413 properties non-compliant; 412 in current works programme","quote":"At the end of the period, 485 of the 3,413 applicable properties did not meet the Decent Homes Standard. Of these failures: 412 are included in the current year's works programme; 43 are to be reviewed.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Finance and Performance Scrutiny Sub-Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - 2026-27 - Corporate Performance Report Q1 - Draft v4","paper_url":"https://folkestone-hythe.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s56722/56722.pdf","headline":"Household waste recycling rate fell short of target at 44%, with prior-year data confirming underperformance.","detail":"The council's household waste recycling rate for Q1 stands at 44% against an annual target of 50%, marked as off-target. The report notes the current position is 'subject to validation', but the confirmed year-end result for 2025-26 was 43.7%, confirming that the underperformance is structural rather than a one-quarter anomaly.","category":"demand","matters":"Persistent shortfall against recycling targets can indicate service delivery issues or operational cost overruns in waste collection and processing, and may reflect non-compliance with waste management contracts.","figures":"Recycling rate 44% vs 50% target; confirmed 2025-26 year-end result 43.7%","quote":"Aim to maximise. *Current position subject to validation. Confirmed year-end result (43.7%) indicates performance has worsened.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-29"},"name":"Folkestone & Hythe","findings_total":130,"news_drafts_total":3}}